# .gitattributes
#
# CRLF IN THE WORKING TREE, on every platform (maintainer, 2026-11-17).
#
# `text=auto` keeps the INDEX normalized to LF, so commits and diffs stay
# line-ending neutral; `eol=crlf` writes CRLF on every checkout, Windows and
# CI (ubuntu) alike. That matters because `tools/engine-hash.mjs` hashes the
# RAW BYTES of every file in the optimizer's import graph: a checkout must
# produce the same bytes everywhere for the meta's engineHash to hold.
# Files a Node script writes (npm run data / meta) come out LF until git
# rewrites them; see .claude/rules/generated-data-locks.md.
#
# History: until 2026-11-17 this pinned `eol=lf`, because a Windows checkout
# kept writing CRLF and moving the hash. Switched once Claude Code's Write and
# Edit tools were measured to leave CRLF after every edit (docs/history/
# 2026-11-17-line-endings.md).
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Binaries git must never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.db binary
*.zip binary
